[{"id":"VRCE-4-10-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":1,"english":"Then wishing for my welfare I strove to propitiate my angry brother, wrought up with wrath, who was seated (there).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0b8a719c32ee6959ed2ec8233e90e409fd89d0ad3e926cdbbff5d24095b30e88","compact":"3005cee86502ecf7201f3eed0c35ce2e4d562ff0c48234b2bd292148da89961f","nasal":"3005cee86502ecf7201f3eed0c35ce2e4d562ff0c48234b2bd292148da89961f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":2,"english":"By good luck it is that you had come off safely; and that you had slain the foe. O you that rejoicest the forlorn, you are the only protector of me who am helpless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.985,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54acdc5d0d2767c2b7edd07b0248ad2721c9d50cba5564293a4499799a84f88d","compact":"ed776e492c5eb9bee3bb7b6b0223430d7a09f774e1b44170130d229cc381f670","nasal":"bf792fd1a818a3e564719d94ea09e5236b6f3b1a8ae252fcd8539f91d0f12e1d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":3,"english":"I hold this. umbrella furnished with many ribs, resembling the moon risen; as well as this chowrī containing hair,—do you accept my service.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23fd4cdb71284b062fcdfacb39965aaecff80e8cc749e6c95fdc119bd42d9f4b","compact":"51acdd865847565f743a7f7b314325b571b036f3e162a09350ff0c5087971c9b","nasal":"5c8fb3cf28e3a11e5a839c0d5fa6008190810a83e1451812839bcbe8d4d00570"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":4,"english":"You are the king, O worthy of honour; and I am, as before, ever (your servant). I was entrusted with regal power in consequence of your absence. This kingdom consisting of courtiers and citizens, remains now rid of its thorns. It was established in me as a trust. And I protected it as such.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c484cb08c4e01279fb31667acb44a0e65308dba68b0b506a68e8856addf93f6","compact":"75248c0f933be2f33243460cd6f222d07eb0d184e2d304a9edc0c26f5081af5a","nasal":"75248c0f933be2f33243460cd6f222d07eb0d184e2d304a9edc0c26f5081af5a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":5,"english":"Do not get wroth, O miid one, O destroyer of foes, I beseech you with bent head, and, O king, with joined hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.65,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0adb956779569e25528a6ef213971bc085e38d6f4debe229dfe9d90a75d448fa","compact":"75910c0e1512a94b044d1729f3ad24c7d205efdb3bfd8be2806aabcc5722d125","nasal":"a23c2b95d3b57ab262c810570bbf56a3c02de0187511468e5d6976bff58a098f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":6,"english":"With the view of preventing any one to wish to conquer this kingdom vacant (of its ruler the citizens and counsellors unanimously, by force, entrusted me with regal authority.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b42a0b951e1802799e748024a98ea19459f67b8a2f7d7273ef8222b31ce0d29b","compact":"aa609251961cf9e09fd86600a79b6b12f8d76bd51499c0029828e57924f91170","nasal":"d297d0ef82650e9e0720c51edf0c4119d052fb5813d2f9d0d91fb4220d66af54"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":7,"english":"As I said this softly, the monkey reproaching me, said to me 'Fie on you,' and censured me greatly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad10f27cc589a5ba4b8778ffa6569be574fd60a5fcbe4e68bdaacdb5559614fc","compact":"96f5830dec29b5e254e8604ed6c2e30541f9780619c90739b9d2258dce2cd881","nasal":"96f5830dec29b5e254e8604ed6c2e30541f9780619c90739b9d2258dce2cd881"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":8,"english":"And bringing together the subjects and favourite counsellors, spoke to me, before friends, highly improper words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d9bc9e6cf21bb8d75ca69a5d7221d57b1fc65612716a743ba47f11dc0457d281","compact":"5b6eef5cccb78c931c112dc2009e5f8d7fbe3f9d179e8a35d66b8eac177d8f44","nasal":"17f272feac2af083c1244c0ef5ed6f032886dd8850209d02686ba2a16d984352"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":9,"english":"“You know that formerly one night the mighty Asura Mayavi, getting' enraged, challenged me (to a fight) desirous of an encounter with me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.569,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbcd9babd9c0bc3069b208a7c34984bcad847cd4fa3f1f799937c888d81e682b","compact":"e1017456f96a2d0924631c5101dabf0f07f913ec43e01f5c35c40314114dc209","nasal":"d4e699ab9d3dcbe09cb42844833fce240b36a4abb5129bfbbb729620e8acc723"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":10,"english":"Hearing his speech I sallied out of the palace, and was followed by this horrible brother of mine.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e305d8296e00a8847003f0ec4076b07b25268058f660f88009da648c3f3b70ca","compact":"8b7185d510c739a799e01c6d251a9cef2a134c238da2d60f785fb336fe3076b8","nasal":"8b7185d510c739a799e01c6d251a9cef2a134c238da2d60f785fb336fe3076b8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":11,"english":"Thereat seeing me with one to assist me, and finding that we had come upon him, that mighty Asura, fled, seized with fear. And fleeing on, he (at length) swiftly entered a huge hole.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.577,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"893bf388f921bf02ade09bc3eeb351f1320d85b464ab289862a983f2de772e96","compact":"49c602b3f4595a9e61b96ee17d8f4e5078d69951b47e27d19b8912d92fe37cb4","nasal":"49c602b3f4595a9e61b96ee17d8f4e5078d69951b47e27d19b8912d92fe37cb4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":12,"english":"Knowing that he had entered that dreadful and large cave, I spoke to my brother of a crooked presence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eeb1490174fce7276f7b952d6c43e6db0149328b44231bd2350e872055d9b8c9","compact":"4056d961d34b208b3eab29727373f3b0d4022a6e49dbbc6bc03b5c8f6a793145","nasal":"4056d961d34b208b3eab29727373f3b0d4022a6e49dbbc6bc03b5c8f6a793145"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":13,"english":"Without slaying (this Asura) I cannot return to the palace. Do you wait at the mouth of the cave while I slay him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aaa2a756a01df317b80de43c2b44e296883c43bb63b87e4dee9ba283527d6986","compact":"8803535c862786ff64a554168b44e6af74bfb255dfddd85fd72fd32c8583247a","nasal":"31f37de5efde400398ac8f766879bb6739b496bc2e608bb6a24f63992fd45340"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":14,"english":"This one is stationed here-thinking thus, I entered that inaccessible cave. And as I searched (for the Asura), one entire year passed away.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.344,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f804e5745435400d685a7d450525726719f001664d5e0157f6ab6451bab7e3a8","compact":"dc64a96d281502ef75d499fabc7a53b0c2faac8792e040519629e14cf5253405","nasal":"dc64a96d281502ef75d499fabc7a53b0c2faac8792e040519629e14cf5253405"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":15,"english":"That wicked wight who had roused my alarm in consequence of his disappearance, was (at length) slain by me in one day, along with his friends.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"239dc8015052c0451d3ed0e074605516519563005fa4ef3c067b89868ad16bbd","compact":"a0f131798a158d3d154556a5b1bd7cfa5630f258fdae8d5cc4ded0c3c6e7e78d","nasal":"a0899c066c25c4f0d79fbbdd99a40cd0310a67133cf2d1efadd7cf6e48d02793"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":16,"english":"Then as he emitted yells in the subterranean region, the cave was filled with his blood and it became difficult to come out of it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"538ec27da9b1bdcebef3bdf35f5fe56f363692b662089fe2d37f2183bd32940d","compact":"2b6a4bff31f840649ca68a21f12fb27416ff1df7a3b5f28a7c4bac16238556fb","nasal":"2ab1931fd1a4658c21a12548eac9c5d97b43ea6436b34be5c2eb84fe0d3a6961"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":17,"english":"Having with ease slain my powerful foe, I could not find the outlet of the cavern, its mouth having been closed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.405,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80d3df29ea9d77f6763c7357c0ba094381a609bb60217f8ffb89f47da18a7a26","compact":"8add972c2a29e1034084791e40c4d05516aab4ae600e9a23ef7fab621ea2d80d","nasal":"fb039114e63561c02b610d1764f2fef7996232e145dd0cfe176677537c2c465a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":18,"english":"Then as I again and again cried Sugrīva, Sugrīva, I became exceedingly sorry for not receiving any reply.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd9c009deed389ac2f493170c1cb5eff7ca0dacd8e10bde34965d433ecf53189","compact":"5dd79af473201c9a831cfca185b38952ef3c6256d0bf6ddf08795001f7fbf90b","nasal":"5dd79af473201c9a831cfca185b38952ef3c6256d0bf6ddf08795001f7fbf90b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":19,"english":"Thereat I threw down the stone after striking it many times with my legs. Then coming out by its mouth, I have come to this city.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.475,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fb3449308aa8a1fea791be7525ebdf58ac538d6f889c6b560c0eefb1ed17c19","compact":"d6f7c87e16279dfce4c96a8833b91cf6dabb783ad88a16e821b181392bec857f","nasal":"d6f7c87e16279dfce4c96a8833b91cf6dabb783ad88a16e821b181392bec857f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":20,"english":"Seeking my kingdom, the crafty Sugrīva had shut me up there forgetting fraternal love.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16f54201a81e34d5892502ac9d8f6ec45548b8328268e9f3a93b17848fc7baac","compact":"dbb56af9ebba413e0ad86ffa251dd5fc65d1875adc260530aa0f7d1db3e70413","nasal":"dbb56af9ebba413e0ad86ffa251dd5fc65d1875adc260530aa0f7d1db3e70413"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":21,"english":"Saying this, that monkey, the shameless Vali, exiled me with a single cloth on.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4e3fd6ffc7b64828a81a5fc34be06bf70d5fc56de3c1d90bf7d9849862dfb0e","compact":"c7e04bdc5a5abe7ea5e962f22eb0031f2da8abd7df719310248a60760aca4ecf","nasal":"c7e04bdc5a5abe7ea5e962f22eb0031f2da8abd7df719310248a60760aca4ecf"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":22,"english":"O Rāghava, I have been discomfited by him, and been deprived of my wife. And from fear of him, I have wandered over the whole earth having forest and seas. And aggrieved in consequence of my having been deprived of my wife. I have (at length) entered this best of mountains, Rsyamuka, which for a certain reason* is incapable of being approached by Vali. *In consequence of Matanga's curse.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.483,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09f602e82daa54c35e97b2b4f1467a8b859ef43b6c524ca29bf1fe7f36420ab6","compact":"ff754d136c7a2ac30fa37870f3bbd9c650e84bf27d2e94d64c53253ca095fe4a","nasal":"28b52f9fabe3022900262cea875438c716f27acf51eb51550ede4cb2f1394521"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":23,"english":"O Rāghava, I have been discomfited by him, and been deprived of my wife. And from fear of him, I have wandered over the whole earth having forest and seas. And aggrieved in consequence of my having been deprived of my wife. I have (at length) entered this best of mountains, Rsyamuka, which for a certain reason* is incapable of being approached by Vali. *In consequence of Matanga's curse.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8f51f37fa680985901715bbc5bb307e9a48a127059bb8044737dbbee3d04926e","compact":"1195693de0870f73395c48c78df5c46207605b6545bdaccb5ee4b6880ec294df","nasal":"1f26e0fcd8d672ce256c8a383dd27a3bbf4a0794e106a166b99ac0ce529ac38e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-24","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":24,"english":"Thus have I mentioned to you the great cause of this hostility, O Rāghava, innocent as I am, I have come by this mighty misfortune.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010024","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2339f00ef3b4113e227448b814b654fa4956ed1db1826880b3d137621dd6708b","compact":"084d0f7dddab2d94f56195d956a6bb2d8e9424e6e488bf040a0d2374255c3c77","nasal":"084d0f7dddab2d94f56195d956a6bb2d8e9424e6e488bf040a0d2374255c3c77"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-25","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":25,"english":"O you that inspirest the fear of all creatures, by chastising Vāli it behoveth you to grant your grace to me, who am tormented with fear in connection with Vali, O hero.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.617,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010025","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3591acda188f2243df1be82a1a84ed9d9b40fc79369d948cc5ca74a4c9978048","compact":"bb11f7302f45710fcbc501a8c1c57fe893168b5b411f5708b019a147ba5bcf45","nasal":"bb11f7302f45710fcbc501a8c1c57fe893168b5b411f5708b019a147ba5bcf45"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-26","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":26,"english":"Thus accosted, that energetic one knowing righteousness, smiling, began to address Sugrīva in words fraught with morality.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.934,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010026","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e4d8eeeb4d1702a5e8e11abcb9a03227ea3fb3e9314ee8cc8bb3a8a906eefd70","compact":"76b9c4a7d7cd24b52fc6431907c27763b9f19db6e7b3519eafbc6f7f672851fc","nasal":"2352205b112eda973c3e71ec7a5256e4f24e43d303126ee7753a2978433f6446"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-27","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":27,"english":"These sharpened shafts of mine, resembling the sun, and never missing, shall furiously fall upon the wicked Vāli.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.671,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f61a85e2ba7e0e062bc2d989d58c85ddddf468b364060e15d36ffc2d8a2f7ea","compact":"741d953207e1927705d4475ebb78c9a93ea141473008b23a84fe0dc9956968a6","nasal":"a301260be13f890a422784b887818c275392cda34ef67348fa3607aa2a5468fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-10-28","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":10,"verse":28,"english":"So long as you did not see that stealer of your wife, so long only shall the impious Väli of vile character, live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-10-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4010028","sanskritFile":"Ram04.